<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Croatian Parliament</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hrvatski sabor, Sabor, Croatian Sabor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Croatian Parliament, or Sabor, is the legislature of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and one of the oldest representative assemblies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, with records of assemblies of the Croatian nobility from the 13th century. Under Hungarian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule it defended Croatian autonomy, and in October 1918 it declared the break with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>. It became the parliament of independent Croatia in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/croatian-parliament.jpg" alt="Croatian Parliament" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ZericaRibica · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hrvatski_sabor_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
